commit 6933ad2cf916f5b10fa0ed92276153d04d39ca36
Author: Michael Still <mikal@stillhq.com>
Date:   Thu Oct 22 06:41:20 2026 +1100

    privileged: Do not import neutron_lib
    
    Importing any neutron_lib module imports neutron_lib.db.api to register
    ORM listeners (LP #1802369), costing every neutron privsep daemon about
    33MB of SQLAlchemy, oslo.db and pecan. The privileged code uses three
    constants and safe_decode_utf8(); copy them into privsep_safe_utils.
    
    A test checks that the copies match neutron_lib. Making neutron_lib's
    db.api import lazy would fix this for every consumer, but changes when
    the ORM listeners are registered, so it is left for discussion.
    
    Prompt: Mikal asked for privsep memory fixes that can be landed one at a
    time and measured in devstack CI; this follows the neutron.common.utils
    change and halves a warm neutron privsep daemon from 118MB to 57MB.
    
    Assisted-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context, low effort) <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context, low effort) <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
    Change-Id: I6df255020ec9a48b7433c3c61b8c0dfbc811d894
    Signed-off-by: Michael Still <mikal@stillhq.com>

